review_comments.body:
This PR breaks `UPDATE` on DELTA_FOR; the repro fails here and works on the base. `ColumnData::FetchBaseRows` starts at the first updated row, possibly mid-group. Selecting within that group makes `target - target_in_algorithm_group` wrap before `MaxValue` clamps it, asking `Skip` for about 2^64 rows.

Run against a database file with default settings:

```sql
CREATE TABLE t AS SELECT (i % 128)::INTEGER AS h, (i * 3 + i % 2)::BIGINT AS v FROM range(1000000) r(i);
CHECKPOINT;
UPDATE t SET v = v + 1 WHERE h = 1;
-- Data Corruption Error: Corrupted bitpacking segment: read exceeds the segment row count
```

Clamp before subtracting:

```suggestion
				skip_target = target - MinValue<idx_t>(target_in_algorithm_group, target - pos);
```

Eight fast-suite tests also fail here and pass on the base. This fixes them, `select_bitpacking.test` and the repro. Please add this sparse-WHERE DELTA_FOR `UPDATE` after `CHECKPOINT` under `test/sql/storage/compression/bitpacking/`.

